This is a great question. After a thorough review of your code, I found the root cause and a few other related issues.

The main reason the buttons stop working after login is that your event listeners are trying to attach to DOM elements before those elements exist in the page.

The Main Problem: Event Listener Attachment Timing

Your initApp() function runs when the page loads (DOMContentLoaded). Inside initApp(), you call setupFormHandlers(), which contains lines like this:

```javascript
document.getElementById('projectForm')?.addEventListener('submit', function(e) { ... });
```

However, the <form id="projectForm"> is inside a content-section (<div id="projects">) that is hidden initially using CSS (display: none). When the DOM is first built, these hidden elements are not available for JavaScript to attach event listeners to.

Therefore, after you log in and the section becomes visible, the form is there, but the submit event listener was never attached to it, so clicking the "Save Project" button does nothing.

Solution: Deferred Event Listener Attachment

The best solution is to attach event listeners only when a section is first navigated to. This is a more robust approach than trying to attach them all at once.

Here is the corrected setupFormHandlers function and the modifications to the navigateTo function to make this work. Replace the existing setupFormHandlers and navigateTo functions with these updated versions.

1. Replace setupFormHandlers function:

This function now only sets up listeners for elements that are always visible (like the project search and filter dropdowns) and defines the logic for the form handlers, but doesn't attach them yet.

```javascript
function setupFormHandlers() {
    // --- Listeners for elements that are ALWAYS present (or can be set globally) ---
    document.getElementById('projectProgress')?.addEventListener('input', function() { document.getElementById('progressValue').textContent = `${this.value}%`; });
    document.getElementById('projectSearch')?.addEventListener('input', function() { loadProjects(); });
    document.getElementById('assessmentProjectFilter')?.addEventListener('change', loadAssessments);
    document.getElementById('speciesProjectFilter')?.addEventListener('change', loadSpecies);
    document.getElementById('maintenanceProjectFilter')?.addEventListener('change', loadMaintenance);
    document.getElementById('exportButton')?.addEventListener('click', exportData);
    document.getElementById('importButton')?.addEventListener('click', importData);
    document.getElementById('useCurrentLocation')?.addEventListener('click', useCurrentLocation);
    document.getElementById('clearLocation')?.addEventListener('click', clearProjectMarker);
    document.getElementById('importGPXBtn')?.addEventListener('click', importGPXKML);
    document.getElementById('refreshWeather')?.addEventListener('click', loadWeatherData);
    document.getElementById('useBrowserLocation')?.addEventListener('click', useBrowserLocation);
    document.getElementById('useSelectedLocation')?.addEventListener('click', function() { /* ... keep existing logic ... */ });
    document.getElementById('saveApiKeyBtn')?.addEventListener('click', function() { /* ... keep existing logic ... */ });
    document.getElementById('useDemoData')?.addEventListener('change', function() { /* ... keep existing logic ... */ });
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-range]').forEach(btn => btn.addEventListener('click', function(e) { e.preventDefault(); currentTimeRange = parseInt(this.dataset.range); loadHealthChart(); }));
    
    // Health score preview listeners (elements are inside #assessments)
    ['vegetationCover', 'nativeSpecies', 'weedCover', 'soilStability', 'speciesRichness'].forEach(id => {
        const element = document.getElementById(id);
        if (element) {
            element.removeEventListener('input', updateHealthScorePreview); // Prevent duplicates
            element.addEventListener('input', updateHealthScorePreview);
        }
    });
    
    // Form builder listener
    document.getElementById('formBuilderProject')?.addEventListener('change', function() { formBuilder.show(this.value); });
    
    // Document upload listener (element is inside #projects)
    const docUpload = document.getElementById('documentUpload');
    if (docUpload) {
        docUpload.removeEventListener('change', docUploadChangeHandler);
        docUpload.addEventListener('change', docUploadChangeHandler);
    }
}

// Separate handler for document upload to avoid redefining it
function docUploadChangeHandler(e) {
    const projectId = document.getElementById('editProjectId').value;
    if (!projectId) { showToast('Error', 'Save project first before uploading documents', 'error'); return; }
    Array.from(e.target.files).forEach(file => db.saveDocument({ projectId: projectId, fileName: file.name, size: file.size, uploadedAt: new Date().toISOString() }));
    loadDocumentsForProject(projectId);
    showToast('Success', `${e.target.files.length} document(s) uploaded`, 'success');
    this.value = '';
}
```

2. Create a new function attachSectionFormHandlers:

This function will be called whenever the "Projects" or "Assessments" sections are loaded. It attaches the specific form handlers for those sections.

```javascript
function attachSectionFormHandlers(sectionId) {
    if (sectionId === 'projects') {
        // Attach Project Form handler
        const projectForm = document.getElementById('projectForm');
        if (projectForm && !projectForm.hasAttribute('data-listener-attached')) {
            projectForm.addEventListener('submit', function(e) {
                e.preventDefault();
                // --- Your existing project submission logic here ---
                const project = {
                    id: document.getElementById('editProjectId').value || undefined,
                    name: document.getElementById('projectName').value,
                    code: document.getElementById('projectCode').value,
                    startDate: document.getElementById('projectStartDate').value,
                    status: document.getElementById('projectStatus').value,
                    progress: parseInt(document.getElementById('projectProgress').value) || 0,
                    description: document.getElementById('projectDescription').value,
                    latitude: document.getElementById('projectLatitude').value ? parseFloat(document.getElementById('projectLatitude').value) : null,
                    longitude: document.getElementById('projectLongitude').value ? parseFloat(document.getElementById('projectLongitude').value) : null,
                    budget: document.getElementById('projectBudget').value ? parseInt(document.getElementById('projectBudget').value) : null,
                    fte: document.getElementById('projectFTE').value ? parseFloat(document.getElementById('projectFTE').value) : null,
                    fundingSource: document.getElementById('fundingSource').value,
                    riskAssessment: document.getElementById('riskAssessment').value,
                    riskLevel: document.getElementById('riskLevel').value,
                    approvalStatus: document.getElementById('approvalStatus').value,
                    approvalComments: document.getElementById('approvalComments').value
                };
                if (!validateProjectData(project)) return;
                db.saveProject(project);
                this.reset();
                document.getElementById('editProjectId').value = '';
                document.getElementById('projectProgress').value = 0;
                document.getElementById('progressValue').textContent = '0%';
                if (typeof clearProjectMarker === 'function') clearProjectMarker();
                loadProjects();
                showToast('Success', project.id ? 'Project updated' : 'Project created', 'success');
            });
            projectForm.setAttribute('data-listener-attached', 'true');
        }
    }
    
    if (sectionId === 'assessments') {
        // Attach Assessment Form handler
        const assessmentForm = document.getElementById('assessmentForm');
        if (assessmentForm && !assessmentForm.hasAttribute('data-listener-attached')) {
            assessmentForm.addEventListener('submit', function(e) {
                e.preventDefault();
                // --- Your existing assessment submission logic here ---
                const scoringData = {
                    vegetationCover: parseInt(document.getElementById('vegetationCover').value) || 0,
                    nativeSpecies: parseInt(document.getElementById('nativeSpecies').value) || 0,
                    weedCover: parseInt(document.getElementById('weedCover').value) || 0,
                    soilStability: parseInt(document.getElementById('soilStability').value) || 3,
                    speciesRichness: parseInt(document.getElementById('speciesRichness').value) || 0
                };
                const healthScore = ecosystemScoring.calculateHealthScore(scoringData);
                const assessment = {
                    date: document.getElementById('assessmentDate').value,
                    assessor: document.getElementById('assessor').value,
                    health: healthScore.rating,
                    projectId: document.getElementById('assessmentProject').value,
                    description: document.getElementById('assessmentDescription').value,
                    scoringData: scoringData,
                    healthScore: healthScore
                };
                if (!assessment.projectId) { showToast('Error', 'Select a project', 'error'); return; }
                db.saveAssessment(assessment);
                this.reset();
                document.getElementById('vegetationCover').value = 0;
                document.getElementById('nativeSpecies').value = 0;
                document.getElementById('weedCover').value = 0;
                document.getElementById('speciesRichness').value = 0;
                if (typeof updateHealthScorePreview === 'function') updateHealthScorePreview();
                loadAssessments();
                loadDashboard();
                showToast('Assessment Saved', `Health Score: ${healthScore.total}/100 (${healthScore.rating})`, 'success');
            });
            assessmentForm.setAttribute('data-listener-attached', 'true');
        }
    }

    if (sectionId === 'species') {
        // Attach Species Form handler
        const speciesForm = document.getElementById('speciesForm');
        if (speciesForm && !speciesForm.hasAttribute('data-listener-attached')) {
            speciesForm.addEventListener('submit', function(e) {
                e.preventDefault();
                // --- Your existing species submission logic here ---
                db.saveSpecies({
                    name: document.getElementById('speciesName').value,
                    scientificName: document.getElementById('scientificName').value,
                    type: document.getElementById('speciesType').value,
                    status: document.getElementById('speciesStatus').value,
                    projectId: document.getElementById('speciesProject').value,
                    description: document.getElementById('speciesDescription').value
                });
                this.reset();
                loadSpecies();
                showToast('Success', 'Species added', 'success');
            });
            speciesForm.setAttribute('data-listener-attached', 'true');
        }
    }

    if (sectionId === 'maintenance') {
        // Attach Maintenance Form handler
        const maintenanceForm = document.getElementById('maintenanceForm');
        if (maintenanceForm && !maintenanceForm.hasAttribute('data-listener-attached')) {
            maintenanceForm.addEventListener('submit', function(e) {
                e.preventDefault();
                // --- Your existing maintenance submission logic here ---
                db.saveMaintenance({
                    activity: document.getElementById('maintenanceActivity').value,
                    type: document.getElementById('maintenanceType').value,
                    date: document.getElementById('maintenanceDate').value,
                    priority: document.getElementById('maintenancePriority').value,
                    projectId: document.getElementById('maintenanceProject').value,
                    description: document.getElementById('maintenanceDescription').value
                });
                this.reset();
                loadMaintenance();
                loadDashboard();
                if (typeof calendar !== 'undefined' && calendar) calendar.refetchEvents();
                showToast('Success', 'Maintenance scheduled', 'success');
            });
            maintenanceForm.setAttribute('data-listener-attached', 'true');
        }
    }
}
```

3. Replace navigateTo function:

Modify this function to call attachSectionFormHandlers for the relevant sections.

```javascript
function navigateTo(sectionId) {
    document.querySelectorAll('.sidebar .nav-link').forEach(l => l.classList.remove('active'));
    const targetLink = document.querySelector(`[data-target="${sectionId}"]`);
    if (targetLink) targetLink.classList.add('active');
    document.querySelectorAll('.content-section').forEach(section => section.classList.remove('active'));
    const targetSection = document.getElementById(sectionId);
    if (targetSection) targetSection.classList.add('active');
    
    // Attach form handlers dynamically when a section is first shown
    if (sectionId === 'projects' || sectionId === 'assessments' || sectionId === 'species' || sectionId === 'maintenance') {
        attachSectionFormHandlers(sectionId);
    }
    
    const loaders = {
        dashboard: loadDashboard,
        projects: () => { loadProjects(); setTimeout(initProjectMap, 100); },
        assessments: loadAssessments,
        species: loadSpecies,
        maintenance: () => { loadMaintenance(); if (document.querySelector('[data-view="calendar-view"]')?.classList.contains('active')) setTimeout(loadCalendar, 100); },
        charts: loadAnalyticsCharts,
        data: loadDataSummary,
        weather: loadWeatherData,
        userguide: () => {}
    };
    if (loaders[sectionId]) loaders[sectionId]();
    fixMobileLayout();
}
```

Additional Minor Issues Found and Fixed

1. Global Function References: Your HTML uses onclick="window.login()" and onclick="window.logout()". The window.login and window.logout functions are defined correctly. However, for consistency, ensure window.navigateTo, window.editProject, etc., are also properly exposed. You have this at the bottom of your script, which is correct.
2. showApprovalDetails Function: This function is called from onclick="showApprovalDetails(...)" inside your loadProjects function. You need to define showApprovalDetails as a global function.
3. updateHealthScorePreview Dependencies: The updateHealthScorePreview function relies on ecosystemScoring. Ensure ecosystemScoring is defined before updateHealthScorePreview. Your current order is correct.

How to Test the Fix

1. Replace the three functions in your code (setupFormHandlers, attachSectionFormHandlers, and navigateTo) with the corrected versions provided above.
2. Add the showApprovalDetails function if it's missing from your script. Add this anywhere before the closing </script> tag:
   ```javascript
   window.showApprovalDetails = function(projectId) {
       const project = db.getProjects().find(p => p.id === projectId);
       if (project) {
           showToast('Approval Details', `Status: ${project.approvalStatus || 'pending'}<br>Comments: ${project.approvalComments || 'None'}`, 'info');
       }
   };
   ```
3. Reload the page. Log in as any user. You should now be able to navigate to the "Projects" section and successfully save a new project. The "Save Project" button will now work.

This approach ensures that event listeners are attached only when the user actually needs to interact with a specific form, making the application more reliable and performant.
